From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 22:34:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132: describe the ProRes encoder
 and its DART

Describe the T8132 ProRes engine (APR) and its DART from the J604 ADT,
both disabled. The engine's three register windows are listed in ADT
order and not named, since their roles are not known; the driver matches
the node but stays probe only. Its power state is SCODEC (the ADT clock
gate SCODEC-V is a child of it). The DART has no power gate of its own and
is put in the same domain, so it is on whenever it is touched, as the AVE
DARTs are.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
(cherry picked from commit 343dfc5259d85e0dee1574774eb19057d37fcb36)
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi | 33 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 33 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi
index 612edce266..2d5469b842 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi
@@ -915,6 +915,39 @@
 			status = "disabled";
 		};
 
+		/*
+		 * ProRes encoder (APR): J604 runtime ADT apr and dart-apr. apr has
+		 * three register windows whose roles are not known (not named), irqs
+		 * 1147 and 1184, and the clock gates PRORES-SOC-VNOM/VMAX
+		 * (performance states) and SCODEC-V, a child of SCODEC: its power
+		 * state is ps_scodec. dart-apr: irq 1146, stream 1 (mapper-apr),
+		 * vm-base 0x10000000000, vm-size 0x30000000000 and no power gate of
+		 * its own: it is put in SCODEC so it is on whenever it is touched.
+		 */
+		apr: video-codec@281000000 {
+			compatible = "apple,t8132-prores", "apple,prores";
+			reg = <0x2 0x81000000 0x0 0x4000>,
+			      <0x2 0x80000000 0x0 0x1000000>,
+			      <0x2 0x810c0000 0x0 0x4000>;
+			interrupt-parent = <&aic>;
+			interrupts = <AIC_IRQ 1147 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,
+				     <AIC_IRQ 1184 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+			power-domains = <&ps_scodec>;
+			iommus = <&apr_dart 1>;
+			status = "disabled";
+		};
+
+		apr_dart: iommu@281020000 {
+			compatible = "apple,t8132-dart", "apple,t8110-dart";
+			reg = <0x2 0x81020000 0x0 0xc000>;
+			interrupt-parent = <&aic>;
+			interrupts = <AIC_IRQ 1146 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+			#iommu-cells = <1>;
+			apple,dma-range = <0x100 0x0 0x300 0x0>;
+			power-domains = <&ps_scodec>;
+			status = "disabled";
+		};
+
 		/*
 		 * The SEP DART's input aperture is the BIT(40) alias the DART
 		 * translates (ADT vm-base-0 0x10000004000).
